{"name":"Palisade Orchid","hex":"#af8ea5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"palisade","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long, strong stake, one end of which is set firmly in the ground, and the other sharpened.","A wall of wooden stakes, used as a defensive barrier."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To equip with a palisade."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/palisade"},{"term":"orchid","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of the orchid family (Orchidaceae), bearing unusually-shaped flowers of beautiful colours. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A light bluish-red, violet-red or purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a light purple colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orchid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Palisade","blocks":[{"text":"A palisade, sometimes called a stakewall or a paling, is typically a row of closely placed, high vertical standing tree trunks or wooden or iron stakes used as a fence for enclosure or as a defensive wall. Palisades can form a stockade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/St_Fagans_Celtic_village_palisade.jpg/330px-St_Fagans_Celtic_village_palisade.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palisade","wikidata":"Q90685"},{"title":"Orchid","blocks":[{"text":"Orchids are plants that belong to the family Orchidaceae, a diverse and widespread group of flowering plants with blooms that are often colourful and fragrant. Orchids are cosmopolitan plants, living in diverse habitats on every continent except Antarctica. The world's richest diversity of orchid genera and species is in the tropics. Many species are epiphytes, living on trees. The flowers and their pollination mechanisms are highly specialized, attracting insect pollinators by colour, pattern, scent, pheromones, and sometimes by mimicking female insects. Orchids have very small seeds, relying on fungal partners for germination. Some orchids have no leaves, either photosynthesizing with their roots or relying entirely on fungal partners for food."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg/330px-Plant_Orchid_Cymbidium_aloifolium_P1110661_05_-_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid","wikidata":"Q25308"},{"title":"Orchid (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Orchid is a bright rich purple color that resembles the color which various orchids often exhibit."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Labiata.jpg/330px-Labiata.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orchid_(color)","wikidata":"Q1925148"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG/500px-Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG/500px-Museumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Reconstruction of a medieval palisade in Germany","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMuseumdorf_D%C3%BCppel2.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg/500px-Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg/500px-Chromesun_kincaid_site_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Kincaid site, a Mississippian culture palisaded settlement in southern Illinois","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChromesu